Hello,

The estimated effort for this SALMA enhancement is **18 person-days**.

The feature will allow users to configure, for each institution, whether payment descriptions are **read from the uploaded Excel file** or **entered manually in the application**.

The expected behavior is:

- **Read from Excel:** Users configure which Excel column contains the payment description. The application reads the description for each payment, and manual description entry is disabled in the file validation screen.
- **Enter manually:** When no description column is configured, the application keeps its current behavior.
- **Reject incomplete files:** When reading descriptions from Excel is enabled, an empty description cell on any payment row causes the **entire file to be rejected**, with a clear explanation. The file cannot proceed through the application.
- **Retain descriptions throughout processing:** Each description read from Excel must be saved and carried through all relevant payment processing steps.

The proposed effort breakdown is:

| Work item | Scope | Person-days |
|---|---|---:|
| Requirements and impact review | Confirm the configuration rules and identify all affected screens, services, database structures and processing steps. | 1 |
| Institution configuration screen | Add the description source option and the configuration of the Excel column to read. | 2 |
| Backend services | Modify existing endpoints and add the necessary endpoints to manage the configuration and handle payment descriptions. | 3 |
| Database and processing updates | Update the affected database tables and structures, together with the related processing logic, so descriptions are stored and retained throughout the payment process. | 4 |
| File validation screen | Apply the institution’s configuration, disable manual description entry when reading from Excel, and preserve the current behavior otherwise. | 2 |
| Excel checks and file rejection | Read descriptions from the configured column and update the rejection checks to block any file containing a payment with an empty description. | 2 |
| Testing and corrections | Test both configuration modes, file rejection, description retention throughout processing, and existing functionality. Resolve identified issues. | 3 |
| Release preparation and handover | Prepare database update scripts, release instructions and a brief explanation of the new configuration. | 1 |
| **Total estimated effort** | | **18** |

This estimate covers the complete change across the application, database and payment processing flow.
